WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.426
The next night started as an ordinary Friday evening, even though it was the last time Mr. and Mrs. Darling saw their three children for a very long time.

2
00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:18.748
They were dressing for a dinner party, and Mrs. Darling was helping her husband tie his bow tie.

3
00:00:18.749 --> 00:00:23.801
She looked splendid in her white evening gown and a necklace George had given her.

4
00:00:23.802 --> 00:00:28.518
She told her husband about seeing Peter in the nursery the night before.

5
00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:34.216
When she described how Nana had caught his shadow, Mr. Darling laughed at the story.

6
00:00:34.217 --> 00:00:42.980
But when she took him to the nursery and showed him the shadow, which she had carefully folded and put in a drawer, he almost believed her.

7
00:00:42.981 --> 00:00:46.718
Meanwhile, Nana was getting the children ready for bed.

8
00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:51.028
As the baby of the family, Michael sometimes made a fuss.

9
00:00:51.029 --> 00:00:57.066
"I won't take a bath! I won't! And I won't go to bed!" he would shout.

10
00:00:57.067 --> 00:01:02.817
Tonight, when it came time for his medicine, Michael refused to take it.

11
00:01:02.818 --> 00:01:10.886
Michael ran from the bathroom into the nursery, and Nana followed with his spoonful of medicine held carefully between her teeth.

12
00:01:10.887 --> 00:01:13.491
John and Wendy were right behind.

13
00:01:13.492 --> 00:01:21.764
When Mr. and Mrs. Darling saw the problem, Mrs. Darling went straight to the kitchen for a chocolate to sweeten the taste of the medicine.

14
00:01:21.765 --> 00:01:27.528
Mr. Darling was much more strict. "Be brave!" he commanded Michael.

15
00:01:27.529 --> 00:01:31.528
"When I was your age, I took medicine without a word.

16
00:01:31.529 --> 00:01:36.703
I even thanked my parents for giving me medicine to make me well."

17
00:01:36.704 --> 00:01:43.722
Trying to be helpful, Wendy interrupted, "You still take medicine too, don't you, Father?"

18
00:01:43.723 --> 00:01:51.960
It was true. And even though Mr. Darling wanted Michael to be brave, it was also true that he didn't like his medicine.

19
00:01:51.961 --> 00:01:55.227
He often found reasons not to take it.

20
00:01:55.228 --> 00:01:58.738
"It's much nastier than Michael's!" he said.

21
00:01:58.739 --> 00:02:04.682
"And, if I hadn't lost the bottle, I would take it now to show you how I do it, Michael."

22
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:08.764
In fact, Mr. Darling hadn't actually lost the medicine.

23
00:02:08.765 --> 00:02:12.554
He had hidden the bottle at the back of the medicine cabinet.

24
00:02:12.555 --> 00:02:16.309
"I know where it is, Father," said Wendy.

25
00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:20.484
She was always a helpful daughter. "I'll bring it to you."

26
00:02:20.485 --> 00:02:23.573
She ran off before he could stop her.

27
00:02:23.574 --> 00:02:26.504
Wendy returned with the medicine in a glass.

28
00:02:26.505 --> 00:02:29.985
It was a white liquid that looked like milk.

29
00:02:29.986 --> 00:02:36.351
Mr. Darling shuddered when he saw it. "Michael first," he said.

30
00:02:36.352 --> 00:02:39.757
"Father first," responded Michael.

31
00:02:39.758 --> 00:02:43.327
"It isn't fair," Mr. Darling complained.

32
00:02:43.328 --> 00:02:47.142
"There is more medicine in my glass than in Michael's spoon."

33
00:02:47.143 --> 00:02:52.993
"Father, I am waiting for you," said Michael suspiciously.

34
00:02:52.994 --> 00:02:59.184
Wendy made a suggestion. "Why not take your medicines at the same time?"

35
00:02:59.185 --> 00:03:05.060
She counted to three: "One, two, three, go!"

36
00:03:05.061 --> 00:03:10.781
Michael took his medicine, but Mr. Darling hid his glass behind his back.

37
00:03:10.782 --> 00:03:14.742
Michael let out a yell. "Not fair!"

38
00:03:14.743 --> 00:03:19.896
Wendy cried, "Oh Father, I can't believe you did that!"

39
00:03:19.897 --> 00:03:25.554
"Well, I meant to take mine, but I . . . I missed it," Father said.

40
00:03:25.555 --> 00:03:31.481
John looked at his father sadly, and Nana left the room in disgust.

41
00:03:31.482 --> 00:03:34.923
Mr. Darling knew he had disappointed his children.

42
00:03:34.924 --> 00:03:37.479
He didn't like the way they were looking at him.

43
00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.226
"Let's play a joke on Nana," he suggested.

44
00:03:41.227 --> 00:03:46.103
"I will pour my medicine into Nana's bowl. She will think it is milk.

45
00:03:46.104 --> 00:03:52.419
What fun!" he said, trying to be playful as he poured the medicine.

46
00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.805
When Nana returned, he patted her on the head.

47
00:03:55.806 --> 00:04:01.295
"Good dog," he said. "Have a little milk from your bowl, Nana."

48
00:04:01.296 --> 00:04:05.098
Nana wagged her tail and began to lap up the liquid.

49
00:04:05.099 --> 00:04:09.033
The children were shocked at their father's sense of humor.

50
00:04:09.034 --> 00:04:11.947
They didn't think his joke was funny at all.

51
00:04:11.948 --> 00:04:18.257
When the medicine was all gone, Nana shook her big head and crept into her doghouse to lie down.

52
00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:20.876
She did not look well.

53
00:04:20.877 --> 00:04:23.866
Mrs. Darling came back to a silent room.

54
00:04:23.867 --> 00:04:27.339
She looked at the unhappy group and the sick dog.

55
00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:30.520
Then she picked up Nana's bowl and sniffed it.

56
00:04:30.521 --> 00:04:41.586
"George, it's your medicine! How could you!" she cried.

